# Apache / WHM reverse-proxy example for PradytecAI
#
# Place equivalent rules in the domain's Apache include (WHM → Apache
# Configuration → Include Editor / or .htaccess ProxyPass where allowed).
#
# DocumentRoot should be the React build output:
#   /home/pradytec/pradytecai/public_html
#
# Backend: Docker Compose `web` publishes Gunicorn only on 127.0.0.1:8100
# (container binds 0.0.0.0:8100). Host :8000 is used by another app.
# Do NOT expose 8100 publicly.
#
# ProxyPass        /api/v1/  http://127.0.0.1:8100/api/v1/
# ProxyPassReverse /api/v1/  http://127.0.0.1:8100/api/v1/
#
# ProxyPass        /up       http://127.0.0.1:8100/up
# ProxyPassReverse /up       http://127.0.0.1:8100/up
#
# ProxyPass        /health   http://127.0.0.1:8100/health
# ProxyPassReverse /health   http://127.0.0.1:8100/health
#
# ProxyPass        /t/       http://127.0.0.1:8100/t/
# ProxyPassReverse /t/      http://127.0.0.1:8100/t/

# Serve React + static + media from disk (DocumentRoot), not via Gunicorn:
#   /           → public_html/index.html (SPA)
#   /assets/*   → public_html/assets/   (Vite hashed bundles)
#   /static/*   → public_html/static/   (Django collectstatic)
#   /media/*    → public_html/media/ or symlink to repo media/

# Do NOT add a second reverse proxy (Nginx/Traefik) inside Docker.
